{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02663",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.01,
      "end_seconds": 3.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "hello, doctor may I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.21,
      "end_seconds": 9.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.81,
      "end_seconds": 17.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "um, so... severe thirst and passing lots of urine. That's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.32,
      "end_seconds": 21.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.37,
      "end_seconds": 25.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "It's been six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.54,
      "end_seconds": 30.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.14,
      "end_seconds": 34.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "About a seven out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.43,
      "end_seconds": 38.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.97,
      "end_seconds": 48.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Vomiting goes along with it, most of the time. The Vomiting? That's been for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.14,
      "end_seconds": 70.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fever, chest pain or fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.69,
      "end_seconds": 73.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.67,
      "end_seconds": 77.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "on the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.0,
      "end_seconds": 84.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "no, that's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.15,
      "end_seconds": 88.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.15,
      "end_seconds": 94.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "okay, so that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.31,
      "end_seconds": 98.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.04,
      "end_seconds": 108.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I take alendronate, once a week for my bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.14,
      "end_seconds": 112.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.3,
      "end_seconds": 120.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "70 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. It's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.31,
      "end_seconds": 132.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.45,
      "end_seconds": 140.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, my mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.85,
      "end_seconds": 147.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "so, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.32,
      "end_seconds": 156.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "I'm allergic to milk, I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.52,
      "end_seconds": 161.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.17,
      "end_seconds": 168.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.38,
      "end_seconds": 171.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "tell me about your eating"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.09,
      "end_seconds": 181.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.97,
      "end_seconds": 199.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.09,
      "end_seconds": 203.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "I've got thin bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.92,
      "end_seconds": 205.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.13,
      "end_seconds": 209.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "I've had COPD, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.07,
      "end_seconds": 214.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "So, I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.91,
      "end_seconds": 227.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.8,
      "end_seconds": 245.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "Okay: height 163 centimetres, pulse 103, saturation 97 percent, respiratory rate 16, weight 81 kilos, pressure 99 over 57."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.85,
      "end_seconds": 252.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.25,
      "end_seconds": 255.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.67,
      "end_seconds": 260.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Okay, raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.26,
      "end_seconds": 278.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "You are dehydrated and drowsy with a slow, odd rhythm on the monitor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.65,
      "end_seconds": 293.32,
      "duration_seconds": 12.67,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with a high calcium emergency at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.87,
      "end_seconds": 297.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.39,
      "end_seconds": 336.18,
      "duration_seconds": 36.79,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a high calcium emergency is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want urgent blood tests done, that's for confusion and polyuria. I'm sending you for an ECG because of hypercalcaemia. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We'll begin with sodium chloride 0.9%, 1 litre, over one hour, single dose. That should help with dehydration. You need hospital fluids and treatment now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.98,
      "end_seconds": 354.37,
      "duration_seconds": 17.39,
      "text": "I'll also refer you to the emergency team if the symptoms get worse, that's the point to to come in urgently i'll want another look straight away right, that's the plan do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.85,
      "end_seconds": 359.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    }
  ]
}